        "text": "31"
      },
      {
        "y": 24.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 430.9,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Taking root and reaping rewards"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.7,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 184.1,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Parts of a plant"
      },
      {
        "y": 88.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 354.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Here are some metaphors based on parts of trees and plants:"
      },
      {
        "y": 100.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 517.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Seed(s) is often used to talk about the start of an idea or feeling: the seeds of success, the seeds of"
      },
      {
        "y": 112.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 255,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "discontent, the seeds of revolution."
      },
      {
        "y": 124.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 506.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Root(s) is used to suggest the origins of something. You can talk about going back to your roots,"
      },
      {
        "y": 136.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 516.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "for example, meaning going back to the place where your family came from. You can also talk about"
      },
      {
        "y": 148.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 505.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the root of a problem or the roots of a tradition. Putting down roots means settling down and"
      },
      {
        "y": 160.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "making your home in one place: After travelling the world for a couple of years, I was ready to go"
      },
      {
        "y": 172.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 240.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "home and put down some roots."
      },
      {
        "y": 184.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "When an idea becomes known or accepted, it can be said to take root. The grassroots supporters"
      },
      {
        "y": 196.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 407.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of an organisation or society are the ordinary people in it, not the leaders."
      },
      {
        "y": 208.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 499.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Deeply and firmly collocate with rooted: Its origins are firmly/deeply rooted in the 19th century."
      },
      {
        "y": 220.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 514.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Stem is used as a verb to signify that something originates in something else: Her discontent stems"
      },
      {
        "y": 232.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 292.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "from a traumatic experience she had last year."
      },
      {
        "y": 238.9,
        "x0": 493.1,
        "x1": 508.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "bud"
      },
      {
        "y": 244.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 330.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Bud is used in the expression nipped in the bud [flower"
      },
      {
        "y": 256.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 328.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "before it opens] [stopped before it develops into something]:"
      },
      {
        "y": 263.5,
        "x0": 493.1,
        "x1": 521,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "branch"
      },
      {
        "y": 268.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 328.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "He’s showing signs of neglecting his work – we’d better"
      },
      {
        "y": 280.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 184.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "nip that in the bud."
      },
      {
        "y": 292.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 510.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The adjective budding can also mean showing promise of seed"
      },
      {
        "y": 304.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 309.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "future development: She’s a budding young actor."
      },
      {
        "y": 316.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 325.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "A branch is something that grows off or branches out"
      },
      {
        "y": 320,
        "x0": 493.1,
        "x1": 511.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "stem"
      },
      {
        "y": 328.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 329.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "from a main organisation. We talk about branches of a"
      },
      {
        "y": 340.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 334.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "shop or a business branching out into new directions:"
      },
      {
        "y": 348.7,
        "x0": 493.1,
        "x1": 510.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "root"
      },
      {
        "y": 352.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 337.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "We don’t have the blue sweater in your size here, but you"
      },
      {
        "y": 364.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 246.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "could try our Oxford Street branch."
      },
      {
        "y": 384.2,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 451.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Metaphorical verbs connected with plant growth and gardening"
      },
      {
        "y": 401.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 429.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The new boss is planning to weed out older or less experienced staff. [get rid of]"
      },
      {
        "y": 413.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 408.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The government will probably have to prune back its proposals. [cut/limit]"
      },
      {
        "y": 425.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 434.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "At last she is reaping the rewards of all her years of study. [is getting results from]"
      },
      {
        "y": 437.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 513.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Because we didn’t protest about the change, we are now reaping what we sowed. [experiencing the"
      },
      {
        "y": 451,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 340.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "logical results of our actions – usually used in negative contexts]"
      },
      {
        "y": 461.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 383.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The journalists have dug up some interesting facts. [have discovered]"
      },
      {
        "y": 473.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 426.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The idea was germinating while we were on holiday. [was beginning to develop]"
      },
      {
        "y": 485.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Out-of-town shopping centres have been sprouting up all over the country. [have been appearing"
      },
      {
        "y": 499,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 194.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "quickly in large numbers]"
      },
      {
        "y": 509.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 288.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Our business is flourishing. [is doing very well]"
      },
      {
        "y": 521.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 388,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "We are beginning to see the green shoots of economic recovery. [first"
      },
      {
        "y": 535,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 238.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "signs that the economy is improving]"
      },
      {
        "y": 545.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 356.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "A deciduous tree sheds its leaves. [loses] Companies can shed"
      },
      {
        "y": 557.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 366.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "employees/jobs. People can shed worries/inhibitions/weight."
      },
      {
        "y": 569.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 372,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Plants can thrive; so can people and things [grow/develop well and"
      },
      {
        "y": 581.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 394,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "successfully]: The language school is thriving – student numbers are up"
      },
      {
        "y": 593.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 393.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "from last year. She loves her high-powered job and seems to thrive on"
      },
      {
        "y": 606.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 170.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "stress and crises!"
      },
      {
        "y": 617.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 399.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Plants fade, wither, shrivel and wilt when they die. These verbs can be"
      },
      {
        "y": 629.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 389.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "used metaphorically: Hopes of finding survivors are fading. [becoming"
      },
      {
        "y": 641.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 383.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "smaller] Revenues/Donations/Profits have shrivelled in recent years."
      },
      {
        "y": 654.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 374.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "[become less] It was so hot in the classroom that the students were"
      },
      {
        "y": 665.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 385.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "starting to wilt. [lose energy] A glance/look/remark can wither or be"
      },
      {
        "y": 677.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 405.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "withering [make the recipient feel scorned]: She gave him a withering look."
      }
